+Backported from 8.2.36
+
+- CGI:
+  . Fixed GHSA-5j3f-64r7-f564 (PHP-CGI out-of-bounds read and write during
+    PATH_INFO correction). (CVE-2026-129538) (Jakub Zelenka)
+
+- Date:
+  . Fixed GHSA-gr4f-wgx5-jpfv (Timezone cache use-after-free can lead to remote
+    code execution). (CVE-2026-129496) (Ilija Tovilo)
+
+- FPM:
+  . Fixed GHSA-qc49-hpvq-g2w6 (PHP-FPM request smuggling through an unread HTTP
+    request body). (CVE-2026-129289) (Jakub Zelenka)
+  . Fixed GHSA-3mg3-cr28-46gc (PHP-FPM status endpoint XSS via unescaped user
+    and script fields). (CVE-2026-129292) (Jakub Zelenka)
+  . Fixed GHSA-jm4m-qfqx-967m (PHP-FPM epoll use-after-free can lead to local
+    privilege escalation). (CVE-2026-129291) (Ian P. Christian, Nora Dossche)
+
+- Phar:
+  . Fixed GHSA-68fq-fh7h-f8gr (PHAR OpenSSL signature bypass via algorithm
+    downgrade). (CVE-2026-128090) (Alexandre Daubois)
+
+- Session:
+  . Fixed GHSA-fm2m-fjf5-v3cp (Partially overwritten session files can lead to
+    remote code execution). (CVE-2026-126714) (Ilija Tovilo)
+  . Mitigated GHSA-658j-r8rw-q6mx (Session serializer mismatch can lead to
+    remote code execution). session.upload_progress.enabled is now off by
+    default. (CVE-2026-115560) (Arnaud Le Blanc)
+
+- SOAP:
+  . Fixed GHSA-q23r-hr55-xmpg (SOAP information disclosure through malformed
+    array dimensions). (CVE-2026-15353) (Alexandre Daubois)
+  . Fixed GHSA-4646-p932-gw34 (SOAP use-after-free when processing DTD entity
+    references). (CVE-2026-129506) (Jakub Zelenka)
+
+- Standard:
+  . Fixed GHSA-f6gg-rchx-xw8j (Mixed-case HTTPS and FTPS URLs can expose data
+    in plaintext). (CVE-2026-128064) (Jakub Zelenka)
+  . Fixed GHSA-mmf9-xm3v-hg2x (Denial of service through folded HTTP response
+    headers). (CVE-2026-127960) (Jakub Zelenka)
+
